        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "1. Athens's catastrophic Sicilian Invasion is the most important event in Thucydides's History of the Peloponnesian War. Three quarters of the history is devoted to setting up the invasion because of this. Through the step-by-step decline in Athenian society that Thucydides describes, we can see how he chose to anticipate the Sicilian Invasion. The inevitability that we associate with the tragic drama is the basic reason for the need to anticipate the invasion.",
            "block_bbox": [
